{{also|fauté}}
==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|fro|faute}}, from {{inh|fr|VL.|*fallita}}, feminine of {{m|la||*fallitus}}, in place of {{inh|fr|la|falsus}}, perfect passive participle of {{m|la|fallō}}. Compare Catalan, Spanish, and Portuguese {{m|ca|falta}}. {{doublet|fr|faillite}}. Compare {{cog|en|fault}} and {{cog|es|falta||lack, shortage}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{fr-IPA}}
* {{audio|fr|Fr-faute.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{fr-noun|f}}

# [[error]], [[mistake]]
#: {{uxi|fr|une '''faute''' d'orthographe|a spelling '''mistake'''}}
#: {{uxi|fr|C'est la '''faute''' à pas de chance.|}}
# [[fault]], [[blame]]
#: {{uxi|fr|c'est de ma '''faute'''|I'm to blame|lit=it's my '''fault'''}}
#: {{uxi|fr|c'est toujours la '''faute''' aux autres|other people are always to blame|lit=it's always other people's '''fault'''}}
#: {{uxi|fr|il rejette la '''faute''' sur son patron|he laid/put the '''blame''' on his boss}}
# {{lb|fr|legal}} [[wrong]], [[misdemeanor]]
# {{lb|fr|sports}} [[foul]], [[fault]] {{gloss|infraction of the rules}}

